{"id":"word:hebrew:H8392","type":"word","title":"תֵּבָה","subtitle":"H8392 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a box","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to תֵּבָה (H8392) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 28 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"תֵּבָה (têbâh) means a box First listed occurrence: Exod 2 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"תֵּבָה","transliteration":"têbâh","pronunciation":"tay-baw'","strong":"H8392","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8392","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["הַ/תֵּבָ֔ה","הַ/תֵּבָ֑ה","הַ/תֵּבָ֖ה","הַ/תֵּבָֽה","הַ/תֵּבָה֙"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncfsa",23],["HRd/Ncfsa",3],["HNcfsc",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"a box","usage":"ark.","full":"H8392. tebah תֵּבָה noun feminine ark (properly chest, box (compare Late Hebrew תֵּבָה ); probably Egyptian loan-word from T-b-t , chest, coffin (Brugsch, Erman ZMG xlvi (1892), 123 ); &gt; Babylonian word Jen ZA iv (1889), 272 f. Hal JAssyr., 1888 {Nov.-Dec.}, 517 ); — absolute ׳ת Gen 7:1 +; construct תֵּבַת 6:14 ; Exod 2:3 ; &#8212; vessel in which infant Moses was laid among reeds 2:3 (made of papyrus, גֹּמֶא ), 2:5 (both E; ᵐ5 θῖβις , θήβη , compare Lewy Fremdw. 100 ); vessel which saved Noah and his family, with animals, during flood ( ᵐ5 κιβωτός ): Gen 7:1 , 7 , 9 , 17 , 23 ; 8:6 , 9 (twice in verse); 8:10 , 13 ; 9:18 (all J), 6:14 (made of נֹפֶר עֲצֵי ), 6:14 ; 6:15 ; 6:16 ; 6:16 ; 6:18 ; 6:19 ; 7:13 , 15 , 18 ; 8:1 , 4 , 16 , 19 ; 9:10 (all P). תְּבוּאָה see בוא . תְּבוּנָם תְּבוּנָה, see בין . תובנתו see בין . תְּבוּסָה see בוס .","rootNote":"perhaps of foreign derivation;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Exod 2 3","keyReferences":["Exod 2 3","Exod 2 5","Gen 6 14","Gen 6 14","Gen 6 15","Gen 6 16","Gen 6 16","Gen 6 18"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":28